---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How Domain Discoverer handles domain lookups, contact form messages, website logs and third-party links.">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container-pad"><p class="eyebrow">Legal / Privacy</p><h1 class="display">Privacy should be <em>understandable.</em></h1><p>What information we process when you use Domain Discoverer, and what choices you have.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container-pad legal-content"><article class="prose">
    <p><strong>Updated October 12, 2026.</strong> This page describes how the website currently operates.</p>
    <h2>Domain availability requests</h2><p>When you submit a domain to our checker, the name is sent to a Netlify server-side function, which queries our existing registrar API provider (Dynadot). We do not intentionally add your domain queries to a public list or a dedicated visitor search-history database. However, the request and the domain name may appear in infrastructure or provider logs.</p>
    <h2>Forms and messages</h2><p>If you contact us through our form, the name, email address, subject and message you enter are submitted to Netlify Forms. Operational correspondence may also be handled using our connected email and database providers. Please do not include confidential passwords, credentials or payment information.</p>
    <h2>Hosting and technical data</h2><p>Our hosting and service providers may process IP addresses, request timestamps, user agents and error logs to operate and secure services. Retention and access depend on provider settings and applicable requirements.</p>
    <h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2><p>The public pages do not require a marketing-cookie banner to use the domain checker or read guides. Essential functions and third-party services may still use technical storage or cookies when necessary. You can manage storage in browser settings.</p>
    <h2>External websites</h2><p>We link to registrars and research tools. If you open an external link, that provider applies its own privacy practices. Some links may be affiliate links, explained in our <a href="/disclosure">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>
    <h2>How we use information</h2><p>We process information to provide the requested check, respond to enquiries, maintain service reliability and prevent misuse. We do not claim that submitting a domain reserves the name.</p>
    <h2>Retention and requests</h2><p>Message and technical-data retention may vary by system, legitimate business need and legal obligations. You can ask about personal information we hold or request correction or deletion where applicable through our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2><p>We may update this notice when the site's services change. The current version will be published on this page.</p>
  </article></section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>.legal-content { padding-top: 4rem; }</style>
